<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 August, from 686 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-fitna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">686 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,340 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pro-Alid forces rout the Umayyad army at the Battle of Khazir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the Khazir River, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, the Kufa-based pro-Alid forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mukhtar-al-thaqafi">Mukhtar al-Thaqafi</a> routed the army of the Syria-based <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. The victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a> extended Mukhtar's rule over the Mosul region.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alids">Alids</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1284">1284 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">742 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genoa destroys the Pisan fleet at Meloria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Genoese navy crushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>'s fleet off the islet of Meloria, capturing thousands of prisoners. Pisa never recovered as a sea power, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> dominant in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1661">1661 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">365 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dutch Republic and Portugal sign the Treaty of The Hague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> recognised Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, lost with the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recife">Recife</a> in 1654, in return for an indemnity and trading concessions. The treaty ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>–Portuguese war in the Atlantic, though fighting in Asia continued until 1663.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-hague-1661">Treaty of The Hague</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1806">1806 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">220 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis II dissolves the Holy Roman Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> laid down the imperial crown and dissolved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. A political order dating back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s coronation in 800 came to an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bolivia declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sucre">Chuquisaca</a> proclaimed the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>, naming the new republic after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a> became its first president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Kemmler is the first person executed by electric chair</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Convicted murderer William Kemmler was executed at Auburn Prison, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. The botched execution took two shocks, and came amid the 'war of the currents' between Edison and Westinghouse.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US bomber drops the atomic bomb on Hiroshima</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The B-29 Enola Gay dropped a uranium bomb on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a>, the first nuclear weapon used in war. Some 70,000 people died at once and perhaps 140,000 by the end of 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tim Berners-Lee makes the World Wide Web public</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tim Berners-Lee posted a summary of his World Wide Web project to an internet newsgroup, inviting outside collaboration. The web, created at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cern">CERN</a>, spread rapidly and transformed communication.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 6 August <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-toba"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-toba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Go-Toba</span><span class="tp">1180–1239</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-fenelon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-fenelon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Fénelon</span><span class="tp">1651–1715</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-vii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VII, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1697–1745</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/petrobey-mavromichalis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/petrobey-mavromichalis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Petrobey Mavromichalis</span><span class="tp">1765–1848</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/daniel-oconnell"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/daniel-oconnell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Daniel O'Connell</span><span class="tp">1775–1847</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 6 August <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marwan-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marwan-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marwan II</span><span class="tp">d. 750</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona</span><span class="tp">c. 1114–1162</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-the-lion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry the Lion</span><span class="tp">c. 1129–1195</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/saint-dominic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/saint-dominic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saint Dominic</span><span class="tp">1170–1221</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francesco-i-gattilusio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesco-i-gattilusio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francesco I Gattilusio</span><span class="tp">d. 1384</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-of-naples"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ladislaus-of-naples.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ladislaus of Naples</span><span class="tp">1377–1414</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-velazquez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Velázquez</span><span class="tp">1599–1660</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fulgencio-batista.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fulgencio Batista</span><span class="tp">1901–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/forbes-burnham"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/forbes-burnham.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Forbes Burnham</span><span class="tp">1923–1985</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jorge-amado"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jorge-amado.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jorge Amado</span><span class="tp">1912–2001</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
